	<string id="receiver_desc">
		<text>
			In firearms, the receiver (often called the frame on handguns) is the central component that binds all other parts of the firearm together. It acts as the structural "backbone" or chassis of the gun and houses the essential operating mechanisms required for firing. \n\n
